 "prompt_sha256": "52c8da5e35cc5f0e1adc9a26403f0eaab1d43c4c814787311aaaf0b8c61ca342",
 "answer": "To configure the LLM and embedding model globally in the current version of LlamaIndex, you will use the `Settings` object. This object allows you to set global defaults for various components, including the embedding model, which will be used throughout your application. Here's how you can configure them:\n\n1. **Set the Global Embedding Model:**\n\n   You can set a specific embedding model by assigning it to `Settings.embed_model`. This model will be used for embedding documents during index construction and for embedding queries.\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.embeddings.openai import OpenAIEmbedding\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   # Set a specific OpenAI embedding model\n   Settings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding(model=\"text-embedding-3-small\")\n   ```\n\n2. **Set the Global LLM Model:**\n\n   Similarly, you can configure a global LLM by setting it in the `Settings` object. Although the specific method for setting an LLM is not detailed in the provided context, typically, you would assign an instance of a specific LLM class to a relevant attribute in `Settings`.\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.llms.openai import OpenAI\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   # Set a specific OpenAI LLM model\n   Settings.llm = OpenAI(api_key=\"your-api-key\", model=\"gpt-3.5-turbo\")\n   ```\n\nThese configurations ensure that the specified embedding and LLM models are used as defaults across your LlamaIndex application. If you need to use different models for specific tasks or indices, you can override these settings locally in those contexts.\n\nMake sure to replace `\"text-embedding-3-small\"` and `\"gpt-3.5-turbo\"` with the actual models you intend to use, and replace `\"your-api-key\"` with your actual API key if required.",
